cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DiAGRI in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DiAGRI: an agentic research system for plant-growth experiments"
abstract: >-
  DiAGRI takes a research question through a whole plant-growth experiment.
  Language-model agents design the study, analyse the result and audit the
  records; deterministic programs run the approved plan on a grow tent and
  watch over it. Every reading, write, approval and report is kept, so the
  study can be traced and repeated. A person approves each run sheet before
  anything touches the plants, and no safety check depends on a model.
authors:
  - name: "DiAGRI contributors"
version: "0.2.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kirinhcl/diagri"
keywords:
  - research automation
  - plant growth experiments
  - controlled environment agriculture
  - language-model agents
  - reproducibility
  - Model Context Protocol
